    '|b||In Sweden, Carl Mellström and Magnus Johannesson invited people to come in for the donor health check. Some were offered fifty kronor. How many women came?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9440
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:17szi9l'
    '|b||Drag the ''Paid 50 kr'' bar to your guess.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:agy136'
    '|a||Among women, the share who came fell from fifty-two to thirty percent. Men barely changed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||So Titmuss was right? But when the women could hand the fifty kronor to charity, the share went back to fifty-three.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1jhtis7'
    '|a||So the money mattered for what it said, not for what it paid.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:gc2dr7'
    '|a||But bigger tests with real donors point the other way. Nicola Lacetera, Mario Macis and Robert Slonim reviewed rewards in four countries, and eighteen of nineteen raised donations.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1n6wg0b'
    '|b||Mostly gift cards, T-shirts and lottery tickets, not cash. And no sign the blood got less safe, though some donors simply switched from one drive to another.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:oooiss'
    '|a||The safety worry was real in Titmuss''s day: paid blood carried more hepatitis, and since 1978 American blood is labelled paid or volunteer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:mvfv0r'
    '|a||And plasma? America pays its donors and supplies about two thirds of the world''s plasma for medicines.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:111jwxp'
    '|a||So how sure are we? That rewards raise blood donations: mostly agreed. That cash for whole blood does no harm: contested.':
